cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VisualTaste or its evaluation method, please cite it as below."
title: "VisualTaste: a local image recommender that learns visual taste from swipes"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: not0aag
repository-code: "https://github.com/not0aag/VisualTaste"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-01
keywords:
  - recommender systems
  - Thompson sampling
  - contextual bandits
  - image embeddings
  - SigLIP 2
  - DINOv2
  - offline evaluation
abstract: >-
  A single-user, fully local image recommender built as a ladder of seven
  rungs, from cold start, Rocchio and kNN to logistic regression, Thompson
  sampling with diversity reranking, multi-interest modelling and a neural
  ranker, over SigLIP 2 and DINOv2 embeddings of 50,000 openly licensed
  photographs. Each rung is evaluated against the one below it with a
  planted-taste simulator, paired seeds, bootstrap intervals and sign tests.
